 "title": "Smart Bulbs vs Smart Switches: The Mistake Everyone Makes #shorts",
 "beats": [
  {
   "text": "The most common smart lighting mistake? Putting smart bulbs on a regular wall switch."
  },
  {
   "text": "Someone flips the switch off, the bulb loses power, and every schedule and voice command stops working."
  },
  {
   "text": "The fix is a smart switch or dimmer. It replaces the wall switch, so the light works from the wall, the app, and your voice."
  },
  {
   "text": "That's why we install a lot of Lutron Caseta. The dimmers don't need a neutral wire, so they work in most older homes."
  },
  {
   "text": "Smart bulbs still have a place. Use them in lamps, or when you want color, like Philips Hue."
  },
  {
